---
import NeuronExplorer from "./NeuronExplorer.astro";
---

<section class="hero" id="about" aria-labelledby="hero-name">
  <NeuronExplorer />
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "CreativeWork",
      "name": "Interactive rendering of mouse visual cortex",
      "description": "Simplified and color-coded MICrONS neuron reconstructions with simulated activity.",
      "creditText": "Anatomical data from the MICrONS Consortium",
      "isBasedOn": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-08790-w",
      "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
    }
  </script>
  <div class="shell hero-inner">
    <h1 id="hero-name">Mranmay <em>Shetty</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p>
        I’m a research assistant in <a href="https://rossilab.iit.it/">Federico Rossi’s lab</a>
        at the Istituto Italiano di Tecnologia (IIT) in Rovereto. I use <a href="https://www.microns-explorer.org/">MICrONS</a> to study
        which visual inputs reach different branches of a neuron in mouse visual cortex.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also collaborate with <a href="https://kreimanlab.com/">Gabriel Kreiman</a>
        at Harvard Medical School on computational models of visual working memory.
      </p>
      <p>
        During my MSc at the University of Côte d’Azur, I worked on spike inference and
        motif discovery in two-photon calcium recordings with <a href="https://laurentperrinet.github.io/">Laurent Perrinet</a>
        at the Institut de Neurosciences de la Timone (CNRS) and
        <a href="https://team.inria.fr/biovision/bruno-cessac/">Bruno Cessac</a> at Inria.
        Before that,
        I worked on applied AI with <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Aa6m2TkAAAAJ">Rahee Walambe</a>
        at SCAAI in Pune. My Erdős number is 3.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-links">
      <a class="button solid" href="/cv/">View CV</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
